      "path": "_m/d/6/n/u/queen-emma-bridge-wp/curacao-queen-emma-bridge-3906.jpg",
      "filename": "Curaçao - Queen Emma Bridge (3906167693).jpg",
      "caption": "Queen Emma Bridge in Willemstad was opened in 1888.  It was rebuilt in 1939, and again in 2005-2006.  It is a pontoon bridge across St. Anna Bay, and now is for pedestrians.  It swings open to let ships enter and leave.  Punda, the core of the city, is on the left, and Otrobanda is on the right.  The two tankers on the horizon may be waiting to enter the harbor.  I took this photo from a high deck on the cruise ship.",
