    {
      "path": "_m/d/6/n/u/queen-emma-bridge-wp/curacao-queen-emma-bridge-open-1.jpg",
      "filename": "Curaçao - Queen Emma Bridge Opening (3899163192).jpg",
      "caption": "Queen Emma bridge in Willemstad was opened in 1888.  It is a pontoon bridge across St. Anna Bay, and swings open to let ships enter and leave.  It is for pedestrians only.  The bridge was rebuilt in 1939, and again in 2005-2006.  This bridge swings from the Otrobanda (west) side.  I took this photo from the Punda side  (east), by the downtown area.  The bridgeis partly open, and will continue to swing until it is secured at the far side.  It is driven by diesel engines at this end.",
